\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Absolute relative stage-voltage error against the independent 64-interval nonlinear reference. Stage numbering is hot to cold. The affine-temperature assumption omits Joule/Thomson-driven profile curvature; the direct nonlinear calculation substantially reduces that approximation error. These are numerical comparisons using research-specimen laws, not measurements of a device.}}{21}{figure.15}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {13}Candidate enclosure and preliminary exchange geometry}{22}{section.13}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces Left: central $y=0.15$\,mm sections of native candidate cap/window tetrahedra and the corrected solid stack, with geometric voids retained; the flange extends outside this view. The native enclosure is a separately meshed fixture, not a conformal addition to the coupled solid field. Right: the explicitly filled stepped-core geometry used only by the preliminary exchange operator. The native surfaces and proxy surfaces are different models. Neither panel is a newly solved enclosure temperature field.}}{22}{figure.16}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {13.1}Gray radiation and pressure-dependent gas network}{23}{subsection.13.1}\protected@file@percent }
